  //
  // Three sentences here are the difference between a true screen and an
  // alarming one, so they are translated as claims rather than as labels:
  // owed.undated says an invoice with NO due date is not overdue (it is a
  // separate sentence, never a rung on the aging ladder); owed.credits says an
  // overpayment is money the contractor HOLDS, not money owed to them; and
  // revenue.caption says payments received are a DIFFERENT measure from the
  // revenue tile above it, which is why the two numbers disagree by design.
  //
  // aging.* keeps its own `undated` out of the ladder for the same reason the
  // AGING_LABEL map at the call site does.
