  // ── Estimate accuracy (app/app/analytics/estimate-accuracy/page.js) ──
  //
  // Three measures, named apart on purpose and NOT collapsible into one word:
  // typicalJob is the MEDIAN and leads the card, average is the mean and says
  // so, and aggregate is the money answer — estimated against actual — which
  // is deliberately not the accuracy answer.
  //
  // floorNote is an argument, not an apology: it says a percentage needs at
  // least {floor} jobs behind it and that below that the page SAYS so instead
  // of printing a number. Compressed to "too few", the reader is left with a
  // threshold that looks arbitrary.
  //
  // dq.* are exclusions. Every one must read as "we could not include this" —
  // dq.unratedHours in particular is an hour whose COST is unknown, never an
  // hour that cost nothing, and dq.unratedWho spells out which way the error
  // runs so nobody reads a cheap-looking job as a profitable one.
  //
  // preset.* — the same buttons as the statements and win/loss screens.
  // thisQuarter / yearToDate / lastYear are copied VERBATIM from
  // app.statements.preset.* and app.winLoss.preset.*; last6Months and
  // last12Months are new and written in the same voice. Three wordings for
  // "Year to date" in one product is drift, not variety.
